<title>GERMANY: German air cargo market grows 5.7pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>German air cargo market grows 5.7pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total air cargo flown to and from Germany rose 5.7 percent to 1,985,282 tonnes in 1996, the German airports association (ADV) said.</p>
<p>The following table shows total, flown and trucked air cargo volumes in tonnes at international German airports January-December 1996 with percentage changes from a year ago.</p>
<p> Airport	  Flown	Trucked   Total    Pct change</p>
<p> Berlin(total)     33,783    5,930    39,713   up   14.4</p>
<p> -Tegel		18,747    5,577    24,324   up   10.1</p>
<p> -Tempelhof	     325	  0	 325   down 47.0</p>
<p> -Schoenefeld	14,711	353    15,064   up   25.4</p>
<p> Bremen		 2,643   24,230    26,873   up   17.6</p>
<p> Dresden		1,476    2,851     4,327   up   14.8</p>
<p> Duesseldorf	 58,695   50,352   109,047   down  2.6</p>
<p> Frankfurt	1,366,400	n/a	 n/a</p>
<p> Hamburg	     36,467   28,785    65,252   down  8.0</p>
<p> Hanover	     11,478	n/a	 n/a</p>
<p> Cologne	    322,521   33,769   356,290   up   11.5</p>
<p> Leipzig/Halle	3,069    1,431     4,500   up   39.7</p>
<p> Munich		82,948   67,300   150,248   up    9.7</p>
<p> Muenster		 704   12,482    13,186   up   10.2</p>
<p> Nuremberg	   45,364   30,396    75,760   up    7.2</p>
<p> Saarbruecken	   740    1,680     2,420   up    4.5</p>
<p> Stuttgart	   18,994   53,511    72,505   up    4.7</p>
<p> TOTAL	    1,985,282	n/a	 n/a</p>
<p>*Notes: No overall air cargo total is given as several large airports with known large trucking volumes do not release trucking figures.</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
